itle":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Although it is the sister species of the brown bear, it has evolved to occupy a narrower ecological niche, with many body characteristics adapted for cold temperatures, for moving across snow, ice and open water, and for hunting seals, which make up most of its diet.","title":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Although most polar bears are born on land, they spend most of their time on the sea ice.","title":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Their scientific name means "maritime bear" and derives from this fact.","title":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Polar bears hunt their preferred food of seals from the edge of sea ice, often living off fat reserves when no sea ice is present.","title":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Because of their dependence on the sea ice, polar bears are classified as marine mammals.","title":"Polar bear"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The English Language Proficiency Test (ELPT) was the name of a SAT II last administered in January 2005.","title":"English Language Proficiency Test"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was a one-hour multiple choice test given on English language proficiency by The College Board.","title":"English Language Proficiency Test"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A student whose native language was not English could have chosen to take this test instead of or in addition to Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL) for college entrance depending upon requirements of the schools in which the student was planning to apply.","title":"English Language Proficiency Test"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Until 1994, the SAT II's were known as Achievement Tests.","title":"English Language Proficiency Test"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The ELPT assessed both the understanding of spoken and written standard American English and the ability to function in a classroom where English is spoken.","title":"English Language Proficiency Test"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The test was 