ia.","title":"Sugaree"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was written for Jerry Garcia's first solo album "Garcia", which was released in January 1972.","title":"Sugaree"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" As with the songs on the rest of the album, Garcia plays every instrument himself (except drums, played by Bill Kreutzmann), including acoustic guitar, bass guitar, and an electric guitar played through a Leslie speaker.","title":"Sugaree"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"This is a list of electric bass guitar players that have their own separate article in Wikipedia.","title":"List of bass guitarists"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The bass guitar is a stringed instrument played primarily with the fingers (either by plucking, slapping, popping, or tapping) or using a pick.","title":"List of bass guitarists"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Since the 1950s, the electric bass guitar has largely replaced the double bass in popular music.","title":"List of bass guitarists"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Bass guitarists provide the low-pitched basslines and bass runs in many different styles of music ranging from rock and metal to blues and jazz.","title":"List of bass guitarists"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Bassists also use the bass guitar as a soloing instrument in jazz, fusion, Latin, funk, and in some rock styles.","title":"List of bass guitarists"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Musicians known mainly as guitarists are listed separately in the list of guitarists.","title":"List of bass guitarists"}],"peer_messages":["\" is a song written by long-time Grateful Dead lyricist Robert Hunter and composed by guitarist Jerry Garcia.","title":"Sugaree"}
