{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Alan Faena (Buenos Aires, November 20, 1963) is an Argentine hotelier and real estate developer.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has developed properties in Miami Beach, Florida and Buenos Aires, Argentina.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Faena is the founder and President of the Faena Group.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is a member of the Tate International Committee and the New Museum Leaders Council.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He previously founded Via Vai in 1985, a fashion label, and worked as a fashion designer.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Disco Ruined My Life, also known as DRML, is a fashion label created by Maurice Uzzan, award winning designer from Graniph Designs  based in Rome, Italy.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" DRML is a fashion label that showcases "high fashion" icons such as Comme des Garçons, Hermès, Givenchy, Yves Saint Laurent and Alexander McQueen with ironic symbols.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Many of the designs consist of the original logo, however, changed to give a different meaning while still recognizable.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Wertheim Performing Arts Center (also known by the abbreviation WPAC, full name The Herbert and Nicole Wertheim Performing Arts Center) is a performing arts center that opened in 1996.","title":"Wertheim Performing Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Situated in the downtown Miami campus of Florida International University (FIU), it is named after Dr. Herbert Wertheim, an inventor, engineer, scientist, educator, clinician, entrepreneur, philanthropist and community leader, founder and president of Brain Power Incorporated and his wife Nicole Wertheim.","title":"Wertheim Performing Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Both were heavily involved in development of the unive