{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Fastest Man Alive" is the second episode of The CW series "The Flash".","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The episode was written by Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns from a story by Greg Berlanti and Kreisberg and directed by David Nutter.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was first broadcast on October 14, 2014 in The CW.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The show is itself an spin-off of the show "Arrow", where many characters in the series were introduced during the second season.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The episode revolves about Barry Allen (Grant Gustin), a CSI forensic scientist working for the Central City Police Department.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" During a visit to an event, the event is robbed by masked men.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" This is later revealed as the result of an accident during the accelerator explosion and the men are in fact a man who can duplicate himself.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The episode also shows flashbacks when Barry tries to see his dad in jail, to Joe's disapproval.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Flash" is an American television series developed by writer-producers Greg Berlanti, Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns, based on the DC Comics character the Flash.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series premiered in the United States on October 7, 2014, on The CW television network.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is a spin-off from "Arrow", a show in the same universe.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The first season follows police forensic investigator Barry Allen (Grant Gustin), who develops super-speed after he is struck by lightning.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In his attempt to learn about his powers and how to use them for good, he is assisted by S.T.A.R. Labs' Dr. Caitlin Snow (Danielle Panabaker), Cisco Ramon (Carlos Valdes) and Dr. Harrison Wells (Tom Cavanagh).","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Barry also tries to solve the murder of his mother (Michelle Harrison) by a superhuman attacker (Matt Letscher) when he was eleven.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The murder investigation unjustly imprisoned his father (John Wesley Shipp), leaving detective Joe West (Jesse L. Martin), father of his best friend, Iris (Candice Patton), to take in the young Barry.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The memory of his mother's murder and his father's framing and later killing motivates Barry to put his personal needs aside and use his powers to fight those who would hurt the innocent, shaping him into the Flash.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Greg Douglas is a fictional character from the BBC medical drama "Holby City", played by actor Edward MacLiam.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He first appeared in the series ten episode "Together Alone", broadcast on 17 February 2010.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Greg was introduced as a new Cardiothoracic surgical registrar working at the hospital's Darwin ward.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Producers created an affiliation with long-standing character Connie Beauchamp (Amanda Mealing) and played a short romance.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Greg is characterised as an ambitious, abrasive, rebellious medical professional.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He has "Irish charm" and will often use it to his advantage.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence