{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Danny Boyle (born 20 October 1956) is an English director, producer, screenwriter and theatre director, known for his work on films including "Shallow Grave", "Trainspotting", "The Beach", "28 Days Later", "Sunshine", "Slumdog Millionaire", "127 Hours", and "Steve Jobs".","title":"Danny Boyle"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His debut film "Shallow Grave" won the BAFTA Award for Best British Film.","title":"Danny Boyle"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Boyle's 2008 film "Slumdog Millionaire" was nominated for ten Academy Awards and won eight, including the Academy Award for Best Director.","title":"Danny Boyle"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He also won the Golden Globe and BAFTA Award for Best Director.","title":"Danny Boyle"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Boyle was presented with the Extraordinary Contribution to Filmmaking Award at the 2008 Austin Film Festival, where he also introduced that year's AFF Audience Award Winner "Slumdog Millionaire".","title":"Danny Boyle"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"William Oliver Stone (born September 15, 1946) is an American screenwriter, film producer, and director of motion pictures and documentaries.","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Stone won an Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay as writer of "Midnight Express" (1978).","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He also wrote the acclaimed gangster movie "Scarface" (1983).","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As a director, Stone achieved prominence as director/writer of the war drama "Platoon" (1986), for which Stone won the Academy Award for Best Director; the film was awarded Best Picture.","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "Platoon" was the first in a trilogy of films based on the Vietnam War, in which Stone served as an infantry soldier.","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He continued the series with "Born on the Fourth of July" (1989)—for which Stone won his second Best Director Oscar—and "Heaven & Earth" (1993).","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Stone's other notable works include the Salvadoran Civil War-based drama "Salvador" (1986); the financial drama "Wall Street" (1987) and its 2010 sequel ""; the Jim Morrison biopic "The Doors" (1991); and a trilogy of films based on the American Presidency—"JFK" (1991), "Nixon" (1995) and "W." (2008).","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" His latest film is "Snowden" (2016).","title":"Oliver Stone"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Fernando Ferreira Meirelles (born November 9, 1955) is a Brazilian film director, producer and screenwriter.","title":"Fernando Meirelles"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" His best known film is "City of God", released in 2002 in Brazil and in 2003 in the U.S. by Miramax Films, which received international critical acclaim.","title":"Fernando Meirelles"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" For his work in the film, he was eventually nominated for an Academy Award for Best Director.","title":"Fernando Meirelles"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was also nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Director in 2005 for "The Constant Gardener", which garnered the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress to Rachel Weisz.","title":"Fernando Meirelles"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He also directed the 2008 adaptation of José Saramago's novel "Blindness", and the 2011 film "360".","title":"Fernando Meirelles"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"John Richard Schlesinger, CBE ( ; 16 February 1926 – 25 July 2003) was an English film and stage director, and actor.","title":"John Schlesinger"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He won an Academy Award for Best Director for "Midnight Cowboy", and was nominated for two other films ("Darling" and "Sunday Bloody Sunday").","title":"John Schlesinger"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Richard Stuart Linklater ( ; born July 30, 1960) is an American filmmaker, screenwriter, and actor.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Linklater is mostly known for his realistic and natural humanist films which mainly revolve around suburban culture and the effects of the passage of time.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Some notable films of his include the observational comedy film "Slacker" (1990), the coming-of-age comedy "Dazed and Confused" (1993), the romantic drama film trilogy "Before Sunrise" (1995), "Before Sunset" (2004), and "Before Midnight" (2013); the music-themed comedy "School of Rock" (2003), and the rotoscope animated "Waking Life" (2001) and "A Scanner Darkly" (2006).","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2002 he began filming "Boyhood" (2014), a passion project which took over twelve years to finish.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The film was premiered in 2014 to critical acclaim.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Linklater won the Golden Globe, Critics' Choice Movie Awards, and BAFTAs for Best Director and Best Picture.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" He also received his first nomination for the Academy Award for Best Director, along with nominations for Original Screenplay and Picture.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" In 2015, "Time" magazine named Linklater one of the 100 most influential people in the world on the annual "Time 100" list.","title":"Richard Linklater"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Damien Sayre Chazelle ( ; born January 19, 1985) is an American director, screenwriter and producer.","title":"Damien Chazelle"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Chazelle made his directorial debut with the musical film "Guy and Madeline on a Park Bench" (2009).","title":"Damien Chazelle"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He rose to prominence for writing and directing his second feature film, "Whiplash" (2014), which received five Academy Award nominations, including Best Picture and Best Adapted Screenplay.","title":"Damien Chazelle"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" His 2016 film "La La Land" was a critical and commercial success, winning all seven of its Golden Globe nominations, including Best Picture, Best Director and Best Screenplay.","title":"Damien Chazelle"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It also received a record-tying fourteen Academy Award nominations, winning six including Best Director, making Chazelle the youngest person in history to win the Oscar for Best Director and to win the Golden Globe for Best Director.","title":"Damien Chazelle"}],"peer_messages":["text":" Linklater won the Golden Globe, Critics' Choice Movie Awards, and BAFTAs for Best Director and Best Picture.","title":"Richard Linklater"}
