 55th Academy Awards.","title":"Robert Preston (actor)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor (Spanish: Premio Ariel a Mejor Coactuación Masculina) is an award presented by the Academia Mexicana de Artes y Ciencias Cinematográficas (AMACC) in Mexico.","title":"Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is given in honor of an actor who has delivered an outstanding performance in a supporting role while working within the Mexican film industry.","title":"Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 1947, the 1st and 2nd Ariel Awards were held, with José Baviera and Fernando Soto winning for the films "La Barraca" and "Campeón Sin Corona", respectively.","title":"Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" With the exception of the years 1958 to 1971, when the Ariel Awards were suspended, the award has been given annually.","title":"Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Nominees and winners are determined by a committee formed every year consisting of academy members (active and honorary), previous winners and individuals with at least two Ariel nominations; the committee submit their votes through the official AMACC website.","title":"Ariel Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"John Cohen (born August 2, 1932, in Queens, New York) is a founding member of the New Lost City Ramblers as well as a musicologist, photographer and filmmaker.","title":"John Cohen (musician)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Some of his best known images document the Abstract Expressionist scene centered on New York's Cedar Bar; gallery happenings by early performance artists; young Bob Dylan's arrival in New York; Beat Generation writers during the filming of Robert Frank and Alfred Leslie's film "Pull My Daisy"; and the "old time" musicians of Appalachia.","title":"John Cohen (musician)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" (The title of Cohen's 1962 film, "High Lonesome Sound", has become synonymous with that music.)","title":"John Cohen (musician)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He has been one of the most important "discoverers" of traditional musicians and singers, finding and recording Dillard Chandler, Roscoe Holcomb, and many banjo players, most notably on the album "High Atmosphere".","title":"John Cohen (musician)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Magician (Spanish:El Mago) is a 1949 Mexican comedy film directed by Miguel M. Delgado and starring Cantinflas, Leonora Amar and José Baviera.","title":"The Magician (1949 film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film's sets were designed by the art director Gunther Gerszo.","title":"The Magician (1949 film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A lookalike is hired from an agency to take the place of a magician while he goes on holiday.","title":"The Magician (1949 film)"}],"peer_messages":[""}
