{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Spirit Airlines, Inc. (NASDAQ: SAVE ) is an American Ultra Low Cost Carrier, headquartered in Miramar, Florida.","title":"Spirit Airlines"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Spirit operates scheduled flights throughout the United States and in the Caribbean, Mexico, Latin America, and South America.","title":"Spirit Airlines"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The airline operates bases at Atlantic City, Chicago–O'Hare, Dallas/Fort Worth, Detroit, Fort Lauderdale and Las Vegas as of 2015 .","title":"Spirit Airlines"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The ExpressTram is an automated people mover system operating at Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport, in Romulus, Michigan, USA.","title":"ExpressTram"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The driverless system transports passengers along Concourse A of the airport's Edward H. McNamara Terminal, which is the world's second-longest airport concourse.","title":"ExpressTram"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Detroit Metro Airport serves as the second largest hub for Delta Air Lines, after Atlanta.","title":"ExpressTram"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The ExpressTram entered service when the McNamara Terminal opened on February 24, 2002.","title":"ExpressTram"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Philadelphia International Airport (IATA: PHL, ICAO: KPHL, FAA LID: PHL) , often referred to just by its IATA code PHL, is a major airport in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States, and is the largest airport in the Delaware Valley region and in the state.","title":"Philadelphia International Airport"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The airport is a major international hub for American Airlines and a regional cargo hub for UPS Airlines.","title":"Philadelphia International Airport"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Philadelphia International Airport is also a focus city for ultra low cost airline Frontier Airlines.","title":"Philadelphia International Airport"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The airport has service to destinations in the United States, Canad