{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Man in the Rain" is a pop song written and performed by English multi-instrumentalist Mike Oldfield.","title":"Man in the Rain"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was included on the album "Tubular Bells III" and released as a single on 5 October 1998 by Warner Music.","title":"Man in the Rain"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The vocals were performed by Irish folk singer Cara Dillon.","title":"Man in the Rain"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Moonlight Shadow" is a song written and performed by English multi-instrumentalist Mike Oldfield, released as a single in May 1983 by Virgin Records, and included in the album "Crises" of the same year.","title":"Moonlight Shadow"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The vocals were performed by Scottish vocalist Maggie Reilly, who had collaborated with Mike Oldfield since 1980.","title":"Moonlight Shadow"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is Oldfield's most successful single, reaching number one on a number of charts around Europe.","title":"Moonlight Shadow"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Valedictorian is an academic title of success used in the United States, Canada, Central America, and the Philippines for the student who delivers the closing or farewell statement at a graduation ceremony (called a valediction).","title":"Valedictorian"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The chosen valedictorian is often the student with the highest ranking (highest Grade Point Average, or GPA for short) among their graduating class.","title":"Valedictorian"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The term is an Anglicised derivation of the Latin "vale dicere" ("to say farewell"), historically rooted in the valedictorian's traditional role as the final speaker at the graduation ceremony before the students receive their diplomas.","title":"Valedictorian"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" So the valedictory address generally is considered a final farewell to classmates, before they disperse to pursue their individual paths after graduating.","title":"Valedictorian