 food products geared towards health conscious consumers.","title":"Canyon Creek Food Company"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The company provides its fresh food product line to grocery retailers and a broad range of food service establishments such as restaurants and institutions throughout Canada.","title":"Canyon Creek Food Company"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Twisties are a type of cheese curl, corn-based snack food product, available mainly in Australia, and other Oceanian countries such as Papua New Guinea, New Caledonia, Vanuatu and Fiji, the Southeast Asian countries Malaysia, Thailand, Singapore and Brunei, and the island of Mauritius in the Indian Ocean.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was launched in 1950 by the General Foods Corporation.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The brand name is owned by The Smith's Snackfood Company.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" While originally an Australian-owned company, Smith's was acquired in August 1998 by Frito-Lay, the second largest producer of snack foods in Australia, which in turn is owned by American multi-national PepsiCo.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In Malaysia, Twisties is a product of Mondelēz International, after having been a part of Danone and later, Kraft Foods previously.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In Thailand, the Twisties trademark is owned by Lay's, which like The Smith's Snackfood Company, is owned by PepsiCo.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In New Zealand, Malta and Italy, Twisties are marketed under different names.","title":"Twisties"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Deep Fried Peanuts are a snack food created by deep frying peanuts in an oil.","title":"Deep-fried peanuts"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The resulting product is a snack food that can be eaten in its entirety, both shell and nut.","title":"Deep-fried peanuts"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The deep-frying process does not change the flavor or texture of