{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The UK Classical Charts are three record charts based on classical music in the United Kingdom: the Classical Artist Albums Chart, the Classical Compilation Albums Chart and the Specialist Classical Albums Chart.","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The charts are commercial monitoring and marketing devices used by the UK music industry to measure its effectiveness in promoting and selling albums, nominally in the field of classical music.","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" All three charts are compiled by the Official Charts Company (OCC).","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The measurements are made by collating the returns of sales from a number of well-known music stores (high street and online stores) on a regular basis, and this enables a ranking to be established.","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Most classical artist album sales in the UK are from crossover artists.","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" For an album to be classified as classical in the charts, it has to have 60% of the playing time dedicated to "classical or traditional music".","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Only albums that entirely classical or traditional music qualify for inclusion in the Specialist Classical Albums Chart.","title":"UK Classical Charts"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"KFAC was a commercial classical music radio station in Los Angeles, broadcasting for most of its life on 1330 kHz AM, and subsequently in both simulcast and separate programming on 92.3 MHz FM as well.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" "Only 41 of nearly 9,000 commercial radio stations in the United States play classical music" and KFAC was considered one of the best.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" On September 20, 1989 at 2 p.m., new owners changed both its name and its format, depriving Southern California of a major cultural institution.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" During its heyday, the station was arguably the most important cultural organization in the Los Angeles area, having greater influence on lovers of classical music than even the Los Angeles Philharmonic.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Announcers such as John Conte, Howard Rhines, Dick Crawford, Thomas Cassidy, Carl Princi, Fred Crane, Steve Allen, Alfred Leonard, Tom Dixon, Bill Carlson, Dick Joy, Tom Franklin, Ed Stoddard, Bernie Alan, Rodger Layng, John Santana, Steve Markham and Doug Ordunio were featured on the station.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" For several years, the station also carried the daily syndicated "Adventures in Good Music" with Karl Haas.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Other regularly scheduled programs were hosted by Leonora Schildkraut, Werner Klemperer, and Gussie Moran.","title":"KFAC (radio station)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Women in music describes the role of women as composers, songwriters, instrumental performers, singers, conductors, music scholars, music educators, music critics/music journalists and other musical professions.","title":"Women in music"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" As well, it describes music movements (e.g., women's music, which is music written and performed by women for women), events and genres related to women, women's issues and feminism.","title":"Women in music"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In the 2010s, while women comprise a significant proportion of popular music and classical music singers, and a significant proportion of songwriters (many of them being singer-songwriters), there are few women record producers, rock critics and rock instrumentalists.","title":"Women in music"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Notable women artists in pop, such as Bjork and Lady Gaga have commented about sexism and gender discrimination in the music industry.","title":"Women in music"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In classical music, although there have been a huge number of women composers from the Medieval period to the present day, women composers are significantly underrepresented in the commonly performed classical music repertoire, music history textbooks and music encyclopedias; for example, in the "Concise Oxford History of Music", Clara Schumann is one of the only female composers who is mentioned.","title":"Women in music"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Classical music in Kosovo refers to the art music cultivated in Kosovo.","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The roots of classical music in Kosovo are found in the 1940s and include the time period from the times when Kosovo was part of Yugoslavia to this day.","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It can be said that there is a tradition of classical music in Kosovo, however, compared to other Balkan countries and especially European countries this tradition is younger.","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Classical music in Kosovo reaches back about 70 years.","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Even though in a short period of time, this music has evolved, passing through generations of composers and artists.","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In his book "Zhvillimi i stileve në veprat e kompozitorëve shqiptarë të Kosovës", Engjëll Berisha comments:","title":"Classical music in Kosovo"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Musical composition can refer to an original piece of music, either a song or an instrumental music piece, the structure of a musical piece, or the process of creating or writing a new song or piece of music.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" People who create new compositions are called composers in classical music.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In popular music and traditional music, the creators of new songs are usually called songwriters; with songs, the person who writes new words for a song is the lyricist.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" "Composition" is the act or practice of creating a song or other piece of music.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In many cultures, including Western classical music, the act of composing typically includes the creation of music notation, such as a sheet music "score", which is then performed by the composer or by other instrumental musicians or singers.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" In popular music and traditional music, songwriting may involve the creation of a basic outline of the song, called the lead sheet, which sets out the melody, lyrics and chord progression.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In classical music, orchestration (choosing the instruments of a large music ensemble such as an orchestra which will play the different parts of music, such as the melody, accompaniment, countermelody, bassline and so on) is typically done by the composer, but in musical theatre and in pop music, songwriters may hire an arranger to do the orchestration.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" In some cases, a pop or traditional songwriter may not use written notation at all, and instead compose the song in her mind and then play, sing and/or record it from memory.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" In jazz and popular music, notable sound recordings by influential performers are given the weight that written or printed scores play in classical music.","title":"Musical composition"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Odissi music ("oṛiśī") is a genre of classical music in India originated from the eastern state of Odisha.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Indian classical music has five significant branches: Avanti, Panchali, Odramagadhi, Hindustani and Carnatic.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Of these, Odramagadhi exists in the form of Odissi music.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Generally, Odissi is one of the classical dances of India performed with Odissi music.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Odissi music was shaped during the time of Oriya poet Jayadeva, who composed lyrics meant to be sung.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" By the 11th century AD, folk music of Odisha in the form of Triswari, Chatuhswari, and Panchaswari was modified into the classical style.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" However, Odissi songs were written even before the Oriya language developed.","title":"Odissi music"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Odissi music has a rich legacy dating back to the 2nd century BCE, when king Kharvela, the ruler of Odisha (Kalinga), patronized this music and dance.","title":"Odissi music"}],"peer_messages":[" is mentioned.","title":"Women in music"}
